{"id": "EUVD-2026-86672", "enisaUuid": "6ea46792-5c78-383c-87e1-2acdf05b3790", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: mark a NULL call argument precise\n\ncheck_func_arg() allows bpf_register_is_null() for nullable arguments\nw/o marking the underlying scalar register precise. Hence a checkpoint\ncreated on such a path would prune against arbitrary scalar value.\n\ncheck_helper_call() enforces second parameter of the\nbpf_get_local_storage() to be zero, w/o marking the underlying scalar\nregister precise. Hence a checkpoint created on such a path would\nprune against arbitrary scalar value.\n\nGrouping these two into one patch, as they share the same fixes tag.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/febbb66e682d8328f7c5bcbdd5e4291abab2e858", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/627089c278df58749f25686c6a3caf7e181b5951", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1fe6379e401b8ce0f561cb4d84af2b70b4343c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/69a9ad004ccf5d45e534c7d503f47f643abe64b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a3a10b030c96ea88868ccc060a16827c01eaa5a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cgv7-rwvp-jx5m", "CVE-2026-98019"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1750c69e-6701-3b5b-b1b0-d3cb3d6974c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "3011d82c-6310-35cd-941d-8d556bda2113", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "38acf1bc-1769-39e5-ac0d-ab989dc072d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b5dc0163d8fd78e64a7e21f309cf932fda34353e <1a3a10b030c96ea88868ccc060a16827c01eaa5a"}, {"id": "4b625538-3c89-3c2d-9c08-8052a82311d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b5dc0163d8fd78e64a7e21f309cf932fda34353e <627089c27